--TEST--
a call, a property read and a property write through a `mixed` or `object` receiver outside the places a `[[restrict]]` entry allows throw a `LogicError` with the entry's text, an unrestricted member still runs, and the same access inside an allowed place runs — `rule:packaging/a-restriction-limits-where-a-declaration-is-used`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// This file is the application. It is not in `App\Allowed`.
autoload 'App' from './app';

mixed $vault = new App\Secret\Vault();

// `open` may be called only in `App\Allowed`, so this call throws.
try {
    echo $vault->open(), "\n";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// `$code` may be read only in `App\Allowed`, so this read throws.
try {
    echo $vault->code, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo "the read throws\n";
}

// A write throws as well.
object $box = new App\Secret\Vault();
try {
    $box->code = "0000";
} catch (LogicError $error) {
    echo "the write throws\n";
}

// A method with no restriction runs.
echo $vault->label(), "\n";

// The same call through `mixed` runs in `App\Allowed`.
App\Allowed\Door::open($vault);
// covers: tools:packages/restrictions-where-a-class-or-method-may-be-used
--FILE app/Secret/Vault.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App\Secret;

final class Vault
{
    public string $code = "1234";

    public function open(): string
    {
        return "open";
    }

    public function label(): string
    {
        return "vault";
    }
}
--FILE app/Allowed/Door.nvs--
<?nvs
namespace App\Allowed;

final class Door
{
    public static function open(mixed $vault): void
    {
        echo $vault->open(), " ", $vault->code, "\n";
    }
}
--FILE package.toml--
[[restrict]]
use = 'App\Secret\Vault::open'
allow = ['App\Allowed']
note = 'Use `App\Allowed\Door::open`.'

[[restrict]]
use = 'App\Secret\Vault::code'
allow = ['App\Allowed']
--EXPECTF--
`App\Secret\Vault::open` cannot be used here. It is allowed only in `App\Allowed`. Use `App\Allowed\Door::open`. This rule is in `package.toml`, line 2.
the read throws
the write throws
vault
open 1234
